00:10:27,420 --> 00:10:32,480
Our guest today is James Patrick Kuhn, the HAPI artist.

136
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:38,620
Mr. Kuhn is famous for his colorful murals, that is, pictures painted on a wall.

137
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:44,140
Welcome, HAPI. Our audience is curious about how you got your name.

138
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,840
My initials are JP.

139
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:53,460
In Spanish, they are pronounced half pay, and my Mexican friends called me so when

140
00:10:53,460 --> 00:10:54,620
we were in Mexico.

141
00:10:54,620 --> 00:10:57,780
What inspired you to become an artist?

142
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:00,740
My father was an oil painting artist.

143
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:03,200
He used to work in the living room.

144
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:09,560
One day when I was six, I put some paint on one of his paintings when he was out.

145
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:11,800
First he was mad.

146
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:13,620
Then he laughed.

147
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:17,320
That was all it took to make me an artist.

148
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:19,680
How do you describe your work?

149
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:24,100
My work speaks to the five -year -olds in all of us.

150
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:30,920
Though we become experienced when we grow up, we are always five years old at heart.

151
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:32,900
We all want to have fun.

152
00:11:33,980 --> 00:11:38,700
That's unique idea, which is why your art is so special.

153
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:44,580
Thank you very much for coming, HAPI, and for bringing us so much happiness.

